From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:37:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: t8132-platform-handoff: let a policy
 entry name its machine

The built-in T8132 PMGR policy is shared by every T8132 machine on the
firmware path. Some of its entries describe one board only, such as the
J713's ACIO power states, and must not enable those states on the others.

Let an entry name the machine it applies to with apple,policy-machine. On
every other machine it is treated as absent, as before the entry existed.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 306138912376d7814bfeddba17cc1a6cbdd85d8d)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-handoff.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-handoff.c b/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-handoff.c
index 42990c7119..1be411aafd 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-handoff.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-handoff.c
@@ -133,6 +133,13 @@ static int __init t8132_fdt_node_offset(const void *data,
 	return fdt_subnode_offset(data, parent, kbasename(node->full_name));
 }
 
+static bool __init t8132_policy_applies(const void *data, int offset)
+{
+	const char *machine = fdt_getprop(data, offset, "apple,policy-machine", NULL);
+
+	return !machine || of_machine_is_compatible(machine);
+}
+
 /*
  * Apply only availability/ownership, never imported register values. Only the
  * original J713 loader tree (the Airs') can mark a domain okay that the policy
@@ -165,6 +172,9 @@ static int __init t8132_pmgr_policy(struct of_changeset *cs, unsigned int *chang
 				continue;
 			offset = parent < 0 ? parent :
 				fdt_subnode_offset(data, parent, kbasename(node->full_name));
+			/* An entry that names its machine is unknown to every other one. */
+			if (offset >= 0 && !t8132_policy_applies(data, offset))
+				offset = -FDT_ERR_NOTFOUND;
 			status = offset < 0 ? NULL : fdt_getprop(data, offset, "status", &len);
 			/* Unknown legacy domains stay inaccessible, rather than being probed. */
 			if (!status)
